Hmm.., there are no normal keys in Nethack, just skeleton keys. I
never had any doubt assuming that any function handling a skeleton
key would also be named as something like "to pick a lock". As a
non-native speaker I inspected three online dictionaries to get my
impression supported that these two terms (lock-pick, skeleton key)
are quite synonymous[*], especially given their universal usage (they
work on _every_ door, chest, box) in nethack.

Speaking of misleading code, and on-topic as well; you might remember
that there had been some confusion (at least on my side :-) about the
condition when doors explode in minetown (in the source code there
were two different literals defined for the same constant); AFAIR the
doors explode when the guards yell, i.e. the traps *are set* at that
moment. Now in my case, where *I* locked the door myself with my key,
and the guards shouted, it indeed exploded when I unlocked it later
from the outside.

Janis

[*] CMIIW! The skeleton key has other meanings that don't quite seem
to apply to Nethack.


